{"title":"Career Roadmap · Archaeological Survey Architect","role":"Archaeological Survey Architect","summary":"An Archaeological Survey Architect works at the intersection of architecture, archaeological heritage, conservation, documentation and site management. The role may involve surveying historic structures, documenting monuments, assessing deterioration, preparing conservation proposals, supporting restoration projects and coordinating with archaeologists, engineers, conservators and government heritage agencies.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Archaeological Survey Architect works at the intersection of architecture, archaeological heritage, conservation, documentation and site management. The role may involve surveying historic structures, documenting monuments, assessing deterioration, preparing conservation proposals, supporting restoration projects and coordinating with archaeologists, engineers, conservators and government heritage agencies."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Arch graduate, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Architecture","Architectural Conservation","Heritage Documentation","Archaeology","Building Science","Digital Heritage"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Heritage building documentation"},{"text":"Measured drawings"},{"text":"Architectural surveys"},{"text":"Historic-building analysis"},{"text":"Condition assessment"},{"text":"Conservation documentation"},{"text":"Restoration planning"},{"text":"Historic-material analysis"},{"text":"Site management support"},{"text":"Heritage impact assessment"},{"text":"GIS-based heritage mapping"},{"text":"Photogrammetry and 3D scanning"},{"text":"Archival research"},{"text":"Conservation project coordination"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Archaeological Survey Architect” is best treated as a career specialization rather than assuming it is a universally standardized government job title. Recruitment, designation, eligibility and professional requirements vary by organization and position. For roles with the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) or state archaeology departments, current official recruitment notifications and eligibility rules should be checked."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Architectural History + Heritage Studies","Building Conservation Fundamentals","Measured Drawing + Documentation","Historic Building Materials + Construction","Archaeological Site Understanding","GIS + Photogrammetry + 3D Scanning","Conservation Internship / Heritage Fieldwork","Heritage Architect / Conservation Assistant","Archaeological Survey / Conservation Architect","Senior Conservation Architect","Heritage Project Lead","Heritage Conservation Specialist / Advisor"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus","Expected Capability"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Architectural foundation"},{"text":"Drawing, observation, history"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Historic architecture"},{"text":"Building traditions + materials"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Conservation documentation"},{"text":"Survey + measured drawings"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Heritage conservation"},{"text":"Assessment + intervention"}],[{"text":"Year 4–5"},{"text":"Digital heritage"},{"text":"GIS + photogrammetry + 3D"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Entry-level"},{"text":"Heritage documentation/conservation"}],[{"text":"3–5 Years"},{"text":"Advanced conservation"},{"text":"Project-level conservation"}],[{"text":"5–10 Years"},{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Conservation Project Lead"}],[{"text":"10+ Years"},{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Heritage Conservation Advisor"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Arch","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year